Agent: I don't have a recorded final decision about an icebreaker for your team‑building event.

Here are some common icebreakers — see if any ring a bell:

- Two Truths and a Lie — each person shares three statements, others guess the lie (good for small–medium groups).  
- Human Bingo — bingo cards with facts (people mingle to find matches; good for large groups).  
- Speed Networking — short timed one‑on‑one chats (great for larger teams who don't know each other).  
- Desert Island / Three Items — people say three items they'd bring and why (low prep, reflective).  
- Marshmallow Challenge — build tallest tower with spaghetti, tape, string, marshmallow (teamwork + active).  
- Show & Tell — bring an item and tell its story (personal, low cost).  
- Would You Rather — quick “this or that” choices to spark conversation (fast, low prep).  
- Scavenger Hunt — teams find items/tasks around the office/venue (energetic, needs planning).

